Relevant columns and how they will be used in the requested analysis  

• `date` : filter the sessions that happened from 20170601 to 20170731 (inclusive) and to identify the month (2017‑06 or 2017‑07).  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX` : when a table‑wildcard ( `ga_sessions_*` ) is used, this pseudo column lets us restrict the scan to only the daily tables whose suffix falls in the wanted range.  
• `totals.pageviews` : keep only sessions whose value is NOT NULL; later sum these pageviews for every visitor & month.  
• `totals.transactions` : decide whether a session is classed as “purchase” ( `totals.transactions ≥ 1` ) or “non_purchase” (transactions is NULL or 0).  
• `fullVisitorId` : the visitor key on which the per‑visitor aggregation is done.  

Main conditions that will be applied  

1. `_TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170601' AND '20170731'`  
2. `totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL`  

Below are ten exploratory → progressively more complex SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows) that examine the needed columns and finally produce the complete answer.  
Each query is preceded by a short description.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Check which daily tables (within the range) actually contain rows.
SELECT DISTINCT _TABLE_SUFFIX AS session_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170601' AND '20170731'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Peek at a few sessions in early June that have non‑null pageviews.
SELECT
  _TABLE_SUFFIX AS tbl,
  date,
  fullVisitorId,
  totals.pageviews,
  totals.transactions
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX = '20170604'
  AND totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Show distinct values that appear in totals.transactions (June 2017 sample).
SELECT DISTINCT totals.transactions AS trx_count
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170601' AND '20170607'
  AND totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Create an on‑the‑fly purchase flag for a few June sessions.
SELECT
  fullVisitorId,
  totals.pageviews,
  totals.transactions,
  CASE WHEN totals.transactions >= 1 THEN 'purchase' ELSE 'non_purchase' END AS class
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX = '20170611'
  AND totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Count how many sessions fall in each class for a single day (2017‑07‑05).
SELECT
  CASE WHEN totals.transactions >= 1 THEN 'purchase' ELSE 'non_purchase' END AS class,
  COUNT(*) AS session_cnt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX = '20170705'
  AND totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY class
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: For one day, sum pageviews per visitor & class.
SELECT
  fullVisitorId,
  CASE WHEN totals.transactions >= 1 THEN 'purchase' ELSE 'non_purchase' END AS class,
  SUM(totals.pageviews) AS pv_sum
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX = '20170708'
  AND totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY fullVisitorId, class
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Aggregate June 2017 – pageviews per visitor & class.
WITH june AS (
  SELECT
    fullVisitorId,
    CASE WHEN totals.transactions >= 1 THEN 'purchase' ELSE 'non_purchase' END AS class,
    SUM(totals.pageviews) AS pv_sum
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170601' AND '20170630'
    AND totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY fullVisitorId, class
)
SELECT * FROM june
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Compute average pageviews per visitor for June, side by side.
WITH june AS (
  SELECT
    fullVisitorId,
    CASE WHEN totals.transactions >= 1 THEN 'purchase' ELSE 'non_purchase' END AS class,
    SUM(totals.pageviews) AS pv_sum
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170601' AND '20170630'
    AND totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY fullVisitorId, class
)
SELECT
  class,
  AVG(pv_sum) AS avg_pageviews_per_visitor
FROM june
GROUP BY class
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same as #8 but for July 2017.
WITH july AS (
  SELECT
    fullVisitorId,
    CASE WHEN totals.transactions >= 1 THEN 'purchase' ELSE 'non_purchase' END AS class,
    SUM(totals.pageviews) AS pv_sum
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170701' AND '20170731'
    AND totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY fullVisitorId, class
)
SELECT
  class,
  AVG(pv_sum) AS avg_pageviews_per_visitor
FROM july
GROUP BY class
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final answer – average pageviews per visitor for purchase vs non_purchase, shown for June & July 2017.
WITH sessions AS (
  SELECT
    _TABLE_SUFFIX AS dt,
    fullVisitorId,
    CASE WHEN totals.transactions >= 1 THEN 'purchase' ELSE 'non_purchase' END AS class,
    totals.pageviews
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20170601' AND '20170731'
    AND totals.pageviews IS NOT NULL
),
per_visitor AS (
  SELECT
    FORMAT_DATE('%Y-%m', DATE(PARSE_DATE('%Y%m%d', dt))) AS month,
    fullVisitorId,
    class,
    SUM(pageviews) AS pv_sum
  FROM sessions
  GROUP BY month, fullVisitorId, class
),
avg_per_month AS (
  SELECT
    month,
    class,
    AVG(pv_sum) AS avg_pageviews_per_visitor
  FROM per_visitor
  GROUP BY month, class
)
SELECT
  month,
  MAX(IF(class = 'purchase'     , avg_pageviews_per_visitor, NULL)) AS avg_pv_purchase,
  MAX(IF(class = 'non_purchase', avg_pageviews_per_visitor, NULL)) AS avg_pv_non_purchase
FROM avg_per_month
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

The sequence above moves from simple inspections of tables and columns to the fully fledged query that meets every requirement of the task.
